<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · monument</p><h1 class="enc-title">Church of the Transfiguration on Ilyina Street</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1374</span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Church of the Transfiguration on Ilyina Street is a medieval church on the Trade Side of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/veliky-novgorod">Veliky Novgorod</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a>, built in 1374. It contains the only surviving frescoes securely attributed to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/theophanes-the-greek">Theophanes the Greek</a>, painted in 1378, whose expressive, almost monochrome figures are among the masterpieces of medieval Russian art. It is part of the Novgorod World Heritage Site.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/church-of-the-transfiguration-on-ilyina-street.jpg" alt="Church of the Transfiguration on Ilyina Street" width="320" height="499" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Alaexis · CC BY-SA 2.5 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ilyina_Transfiguration_church,_Novgorod.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
